From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250: make the CPUs' DDR votes active-only

The CPU nodes vote DDR bandwidth for their cpufreq OPPs with tag 0,
which icc-rpmh treats as QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS: the vote goes into the
sleep set too. In s2idle the clusters stay at whatever OPP they had, so
the last CPU vote (3072000 kBps on an RP5) keeps DDR, LLCC and the ACV
bit up while the SoC sleeps, and DDR never enters self-refresh
(qcom_stats ddr/cxsd stay at 0; about 1.7% battery an hour asleep).

Tag the CPU-to-DDR paths QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY, as sm8550 and sc7280
do: the vote holds while a CPU runs and drops when the apps subsystem
power-collapses.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
index 206c5986c..b060dfeca 100644
